# Cloudflare Pages routing. First match wins; a real file always wins first.
#
# Vercel ignores this file. `app/vercel.json` carries the same redirects and
# the same fallback — change both together.
#
# 1. Spelling aliases -> the canonical station URL.
#
#    KMRL and the GTFS feed disagree on five station names and passengers
#    search all of them (CLAUDE.md, search strategy 7). `core/data/slugs.ts`
#    already resolves the variant so a typed or linked URL answers instead of
#    404ing; this is the other half — a 301 so only one URL is ever indexed and
#    the link equity lands on it.
#
#    Both languages, because /ml/station/petta is as linkable as /station/petta.

/station/petta            /station/pettah            301
/ml/station/petta         /ml/station/pettah         301
/station/thaikoodam       /station/thykoodam         301
/ml/station/thaikoodam    /ml/station/thykoodam      301
/station/thrippunithura   /station/tripunithura      301
/ml/station/thrippunithura /ml/station/tripunithura  301
/station/thripunithura    /station/tripunithura      301
/ml/station/thripunithura /ml/station/tripunithura   301
/station/edappally        /station/edapally          301
/ml/station/edappally     /ml/station/edapally       301
/station/m-g-road         /station/mg-road           301
/ml/station/m-g-road      /ml/station/mg-road        301

# 2. Everything else that is not a prerendered file: the client shell.
#
#    All 1,252 pages are prerendered, so this only catches a URL nobody
#    built — a mistyped slug, or a route page for a pair that does not exist.
#    It rewrites (200) rather than redirects, so the URL survives and the
#    router lands on the page's own "no station with that name" branch, which
#    carries the whole line and is not a dead end.
#
#    index.csr.html and NOT index.html: index.html is the prerendered home
#    page, complete with hydration annotations for the home route. Serving it
#    for /station/typo would make Angular try to hydrate the home page's DOM
#    into a station page — an NG0500 mismatch. index.csr.html has no
#    annotations, so the app simply client-renders.
/*                        /index.csr.html            200
